Description:
 edulution-linbo-vdi - VDI service for linuxmuster.net on Proxmox
Changes:
 edulution-linbo-vdi (1.1.0) noble; urgency=medium
 .
   * Security: support Proxmox API tokens and TLS verification against the
     cluster CA (verifySsl); vdi-setup fetches and pins the CA by default and
     documents a least-privilege role instead of root@pam.
   * Security: config directory 0700 and vdiConfig.json 0600 (postinst fixes
     existing installs); SPICE .vv files move from /tmp/vdi to a root-only
     /run/edulution-linbo-vdi, are created O_EXCL with mode 0600, and their
     content is returned to the API caller.
   * Security: SSH connections verify host keys (RejectPolicy by default);
     linbo-remote and smbstatus run as argv lists with validated hostnames.
   * Security: .vdi group configs are validated (allow-list) before any value
     reaches the Proxmox API; VMs in a VDI VMID range without a VDI
     description are never touched.
   * Security: used clones are destroyed and rebuilt after the session ends
     (recycleUsedClones, default on) so no user data reaches the next user.
   * Fix: assignment timeouts compared YYYYMMDDHHmmSS numbers, which broke at
     every hour and day rollover and could hand an in-use VM to another user.
   * Fix: smbstatus was called with a shell pipe but without a shell, so user
     detection never worked locally; the parser now uses smbstatus -j with a
     regex fallback, and the QEMU guest agent is used as a second signal.
   * Fix: stopped clones (e.g. after a hypervisor reboot) were counted as
     available; they are now powered on, and the broker only hands out
     running clones.
   * Fix: failed clones were never removed; clone/VM creation now waits for
     the Proxmox task to finish; a master that ignored ACPI shutdown is
     force-stopped and verified to be a template before clones are built.
   * Fix: group lookups in devices.csv used substring matches; VMIDs are
     normalised to strings; rsplit for image names with dots.
   * Fix: duplicate master/clone builds within one cycle are prevented;
     the service survives errors in a single group and stops cleanly on
     SIGTERM.
   * Replace nmap/python-nmap with a TCP connect check; honour healthPorts.
   * vdi-setup: group-specific hostnames, collision check against
     devices.csv, no USB redirection / folder sharing by default, no dead
     lmn-api-secret.
   * Packaging: build with debhelper 13 + pybuild into the version-independent
     Debian layout (works on Ubuntu 24.04 and 26.04), hardened systemd unit
     that stays idle until configured, postrm purge, debian/copyright (AGPL).
   * CI: lint, tests, bandit, package build + install test on noble and
     resolute; release workflow checks tag vs changelog and publishes SBOM
     and checksums.
